<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53624" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασσ-ύω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ]</span>, 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καττ-</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καττύς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stitch,
				sew together like a shoemaker</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				294b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέδιλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					85.6
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			 (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καττύομεν</span>),
				<i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				178
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>stitch up</i> a plot, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶδ᾽ ἐγὼ
				τὸ πρᾶγμα τοῦθ᾽ ὅθεν πάλαι καττύεται</span> (says
			Cleon the tanner), I know the shop that this piece of leather comes
			from, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				314
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καττύειν διαβολάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.58
				</span></i>
			.</div>
